{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas","id":1557915,"title":"Historical Game Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-26T11:41:33-08:00","id":1557915,"title":"Historical Game Ideas","content":"So I made, for personal use, Dark Age Foundations and Pillars for every mage faction I could (even modern ones) and now I want to run a historical mage campaign. <br /> <br /> But after building a game set in 2006 Prague about dying magic, I kinda need help with ideas. Ideas usually come freely but I'm in a bit of the Storyteller equivalent of an artist's block. <br /> <br /> The idea of a Pompeii campaign came up but I have no really compelling story to set there.<br /> I thought maybe venice but nothing comes to mind either.<br /> I'm hoping for a place with nice historical maps to help me visialize the location. <br /> <br /> Any help will be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T12:25:41-08:00","id":1557917,"title":"","content":"Read Peter Lamborn Wilson's book <b>The Pirate Utopias.</b> PLW is a sleeze but the book is a solid history. The Bou Reg Reg republic is a wonderful place to set a pirate centered Mage campaign. It's a real world crossover between Swashbucklers, the Arabian Nights, and Occult Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> If you're determined to set a game in Roman times, read <b>The Far Edges of the Known World </b>by Owen Rees. Large sections of the book focus on the countries at the edges of the Classical World and just beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-26-2026, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T12:34:08-08:00","id":1557919,"title":"","content":"Know any good maps of the historical Bou Regreg Republic?<br /> What sort of overarching plots would you envision there?<br /> <br /> Other ideas are welcome too but this is interesting though I'm not quite sure how I'd set up a pirate based game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:05:55-08:00","id":1557920,"title":"","content":"My first thought for anything set during the time of Rome is something set around political envoys between Rome and China as well as intervening empires. There were a few attempts and possibly some others that were lost to history. You could use the Tabula Peutingeriana for at least part of the geography.<br /> <br /> The silk road in general is a good historical setting for a lot of different cultures and traditions and it existed for over a millennium so there a lot of time periods to choose from.<br /> <br /> Another thought is a small cabal of the Cult of Mercury using influence and exploitation of events to gain access to other culture's magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:10:51-08:00","id":1557921,"title":"","content":"Wilson includes some maps in his book.<br /> <br /> The Bou Regreg is a river (now long dried up) and the Republic was a small city although influential in Moroccan politics.<br /> <br /> The city lived by outfitting pirate ships (the locals would have called them Corsairs, holy Warriors).<br /> <br /> So you have Pirates versus the High Guild. The Republic would be a stronghold of the Celestial Chorus, the Batini, the Taft\u00e2ni, the Void Seekers and the Celestial Masters. Also, given how cosmopolitan the Republic was, any and all types of mages would be present. They've found Katanas and Aztec relics in the foundations of old buildings from this period.<br /> <br /> Given the historical fact of a highly active Alchemical community in this area of the world the Hermetics, the Solificati and anyone else invested in Alchemy would be recruiting here. There were Pirate alchemists and some of these alchemists settled in the North American colonies of Britain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-26-2026, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:18:51-08:00","id":1557922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557920#post1557920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought for anything set during the time of Rome is something set around political envoys between Rome and China as well as intervening empires. There were a few attempts and possibly some others that were lost to history. You could use the Tabula Peutingeriana for at least part of the geography.<br /> <br /> The silk road in general is a good historical setting for a lot of different cultures and traditions and it existed for over a millennium so there a lot of time periods to choose from.<br /> <br /> Another thought is a small cabal of the Cult of Mercury using influence and exploitation of events to gain access to other culture's magics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Tabula Peutingeriana is a very interesting map. I'm trying to figure out how I could use it and the Silk Road idea. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:20:29-08:00","id":1557923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557921#post1557921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wilson includes some in his book.<br /> <br /> The Bou Regreg is a river (now long dried up) and the Republic was a small city although influential in Moroccan politics.<br /> <br /> The city lived by outfitting pirate ships (the locals would have called them Corsairs, holy Warriors).<br /> <br /> So you have Pirates versus the High Guild. The Republic would be a stronghold of the Celestial Chorus, the Batini, the Taft\u00e2ni, the Void Seekers and the Celestial Masters. Also, given how cosmopolitan the Republic was, any and all types of mages would be present. They've found Katanas and Aztec relics in the foundations of old buildings from this period.<br /> <br /> Given the historical fact of a highly active Alchemical community in this area of the world the Hermetics, the Solificati and anyone else invested in Alchemy would be recruiting here. There were Pirate alchemists and some of these alchemists settled in the North American colonies of Britain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to figure out how I would get a group of mages on a pirate ship without it being too absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:22:36-08:00","id":1557924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557923#post1557923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to figure out how I would get a group of mages on a pirate ship without it being too absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Alchemists recruited apprentices from among both the Pirates and the captives these Mages might have started as Pirates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T13:25:01-08:00","id":1557925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557924#post1557924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Alchemists recruited apprentices from among both the Pirates and the captives these Mages might have started as Pirates.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can find a nicer map of the place, I think I'll buid at least a short (handful of sessions) game around it.<br /> <br /> I'd still need an in-setting story reason and character motivation to get a bunch of mages on a ship but I don't think the players will be hard to convince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 01-26-2026, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T16:26:40-08:00","id":1557929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557925#post1557925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I can find a nicer map of the place, I think I'll buid at least a short (handful of sessions) game around it.<br /> <br /> I'd still need an in-setting story reason and character motivation to get a bunch of mages on a ship but I don't think the players will be hard to convince.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poverty can be a motivation. The Corsairs were religiously motivated to attack Christian shipping. Many pirates were hostile to the Monarchies of Europe. Of course in a crossover between M: the Ascension and M: The Sorcerer's Crusade there should be plenty of reasons to turn pirate. Meanwhile, don't ignore the on shore politics of the Bou Regreg Republic. They were fierce and complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T16:31:21-08:00","id":1557931,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia calls the Bou Regreg Republic the Republic of Sal\u00e9. Maybe there's information connected with that name.<br /> <br /> <b>BINGO!</b> Look under Republic of Sale maps. Modern Sal\u00e9 and Rabbat are vastly changed since the 1600s.<br /> <br /> Look on Amazon for more recent histories of Sal\u00e9. <br /> <br /> Read Lanborn Wilson's book. He explains the map of the city to explain the politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-26-2026, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T20:35:43-08:00","id":1557937,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I'm pretty sure I can find a good one out of these maps. The location feels a bit small though but the high seas should make up for that. Can you tell me your opinions on the factions most likely to be involved here?<br /> <br /> Also, it seems I will have to make a few other short campaigns<br /> Pompeii and the New world have come up too<br /> (I have no idea yet how to make either of these work)<br /> <br /> Update: I tried setting up the player map and Republic of Sale might be a bit too small for my purposes (and taste). Or maybe the maps I'm seeing are too early in the development of the place. It's a great setting though. I'll keep it on the metaphorical shelf for future use.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 01-27-2026, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T21:07:23-08:00","id":1557938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557920#post1557920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought for anything set during the time of Rome is something set around political envoys between Rome and China as well as intervening empires. There were a few attempts and possibly some others that were lost to history. You could use the Tabula Peutingeriana for at least part of the geography.<br /> <br /> The silk road in general is a good historical setting for a lot of different cultures and traditions and it existed for over a millennium so there a lot of time periods to choose from.<br /> <br /> Another thought is a small cabal of the Cult of Mercury using influence and exploitation of events to gain access to other culture's magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to find a specific city to set this in now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T02:04:22-08:00","id":1557942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557937#post1557937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I'm pretty sure I can find a good one out of these maps. The location feels a bit small though but the high seas should make up for that. Can you tell me your opinions on the factions most likely to be involved here?<br /> <br /> Also, it seems I will have to make a few other short campaigns<br /> Pompeii and the New world have come up too<br /> (I have no idea yet how to make either of these work)<br /> <br /> Update: I tried setting up the player map and Republic of Sale might be a bit too small for my purposes (and taste). Or maybe the maps I'm seeing are too early in the development of the place. It's a great setting though. I'll keep it on the metaphorical shelf for future use.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Taftan\u00ec, the Batini, the Chorus, would all be in the City. The alchemical connections get you the Hermetics and the Solificati. The countryside of Morocco has a mystical reputation so Dreamspeakers and Verbena make sense there as do the Cult of E. <br /> <br /> Void Seekers, Celestial Masters, and High Guild make sense as enemies. The Carftmasons could easily be among the pirates and allied to any side. <br /> <br /> But remember, the Bou Regreg Republic is amazingly cosmopolitan. Anyone on Earth could be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T10:44:11-08:00","id":1557950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557938#post1557938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to find a specific city to set this in now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is city maps. Looking at the Tabula Peutingeriana, my eye was drawn to Alexandria Bucefalos, which was one of the twin cities created by Alexander the Great to commemorate one of his victories. Well the other, Nikaia was created to commemorate the victory, Bucefalos was created to commemorate his horse, which died in the battle. Honestly, I mostly noted the city because I recognized the name of his horse.<br /> <br /> Anyways, geographically its a good setting point on the silk road as it likely was somewhere in northern Pakistan. That likely part is the problem. The twin cities were lost so its anyone's guess what the layout was like. <br /> <br /> It might be easier to find maps of ancient Byzantium, Samarkand, or Damascus, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T04:11:42-08:00","id":1557962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557915-historical-game-ideas?p=1557950#post1557950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That likely part is the problem. The twin cities were lost so its anyone's guess what the layout was like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True. Hmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}